#comment A LINK redraw: the Hopf link as two lattice squares, colours 3 and 0.
#comment
#comment The colours are the trace's own labels, NOT positions: the component
#comment listed first is colour 3. project(E) is the 2-crossing Hopf diagram;
#comment rotating by x->y->z->x shows it from a view with 4 crossings (an R2 pair
#comment appears), still one connected diagram, nothing freed.
#comment
#comment The two components are INTERCHANGEABLE (the Hopf link is symmetric), so
#comment an uncoloured isomorphism would happily swap them. That is what makes
#comment this the right fixture for check 4: prove_check swaps the colours in
#comment one snapshot and demands a MISMATCH.
#comment
